It turns out that yes, I am forgetting something. From 
http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/343/weap-343.html#calcdamage :

"# Subtotal A is set to zero if attacking thick-skinned creature with
   item made of venom, wax, food, paper, cloth, or
   leather (namely, a bullwhip). Thick-skinned creatures include:
   gargoyle, winged gargoyle, all mimics, mumak, titanothere,
   baluchitherium, mastodon, all baby and adult dragons (D), earth
   elemental, all baby and adult nagas (N), xorn, skeleton, gold golem,
   wood golem, clay golem, stone golem, glass golem, iron golem, horned
   devil, barbed devil, shark, crocodile, salamander, Chromatic Dragon,
   and Ixoth."

With no shoes on, kicking a mimic or a crocodile doesn't seem to do any
damage no matter how much I do it. Same with a +0 pair of iron shoes.
However! With a +5 pair of iron shoes (the great, great blessing given to
me by the RNG this game), I do exactly 5 damage to each thick-skinned
monster that I kick. This isn't great, but it's better than nothing.
(I do significantly more damage to some other creature, but I'm not sure
the +5 actually takes effect there; I would have to dive the source and 
it's too early in the morning for that.

> Highly enchanted kicking boots are unlikely to be the answer, since I
